Package: winky
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: @HERAUSGEBER@
Homepage: https://github.com/DieSchatten/winky
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.39), libstdc++6, libgcc-s1, libpam0g, libpam-runtime, libsystemd0, systemd, polkitd, pkexec, python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-adw-1, libnotify-bin, procps
Description: Winky: unlock the screen with your face, like Windows Hello
 Winky unlocks the GNOME lock screen with a glance at the infrared camera,
 similar to Windows Hello. The face only applies to the lock screen of a
 running session; login after boot, su, SSH, the console and administrator
 dialogs still require the password. Optionally, sudo in the terminal and
 KeePassXC (from 2.8) can be confirmed with the face and the ✌ sign. The
 check runs in an isolated service without network and without access to
 home directories. Nothing is active after installation; the app guides
 through the setup step by step. Everyone records their own face with their
 own password. Recognition with YuNet and SFace (OpenCV Zoo), hand sign with
 Google MediaPipe. The app speaks English and German.
 .
 So far tested with only one infrared camera; other cameras may behave
 differently. Use at your own risk.
